    "kind": "exclusive_authoritative_provinces",
    "exceptions": [
      "The provinces are playable historical-cultural regions, not claims of exhaustive centralized rule: sparsely settled and decentralized areas remain authoritative through named peoples, confederacies, and preserved entities.",
      "Fine altepetl, ayllu, chiefdom, village, clan, and seasonal-use boundaries are compressed where terrain cannot show them, without converting them into modern states or later colonial possessions.",
      "The Pacific transition is open-ocean navigation and intentionally has no territorial province."
    ]
